	"packageName": "oxlint-plugin-hyper-fetch",
	"readme": [
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "# 🐂 Hyper Fetch Oxlint Plugin\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <b>The HyperFetch lint rules on Oxlint, 16x faster than the ESLint plugin on the HyperFetch codebase.</b>\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/github/stars/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch?style=flat\" alt=\"GitHub stars\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/oxlint-plugin-hyper-fetch\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/v/oxlint-plugin-hyper-fetch\" alt=\"npm version\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/oxlint-plugin-hyper-fetch\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/dm/oxlint-plugin-hyper-fetch\" alt=\"npm downloads\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://bundlephobia.com/package/oxlint-plugin-hyper-fetch\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/bundlephobia/minzip/oxlint-plugin-hyper-fetch\" alt=\"Bundle size\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch/blob/main/License.md\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/github/license/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch\" alt=\"License\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/typescript-%23007ACC.svg?logo=typescript&logoColor=white\" alt=\"TypeScript\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/linter\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/oxlint-JS%20plugin-1c2c4c\" alt=\"Oxlint\" />\n  </a>\n</p>\n\n## 📖 About\n\nThis is an [Oxlint](https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/linter) JS plugin with the HyperFetch rules. It catches typos and\nunknown keys in the generics of "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`createClient`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " and "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`createRequest`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " before they quietly turn a response into "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`any`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": ". Rule\nnames match "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`eslint-plugin-hyper-fetch`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": ", so moving from ESLint is a config change.\n\n## 🎯 Key Capabilities\n\n- ⚡ **Lints a large codebase in about a second** - Files without a HyperFetch generic are skipped before their AST is\n  built\n- ✨ **No more typo-induced "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`any`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "** - Flags "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`rsponse`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " instead of "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`response`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " in "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`createRequest<{ ... }>()`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n- 🔮 **Knows the real generics** - Accepts every key of "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`RequestGenericType`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": ", including "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`params`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n- 🧩 **Handles composed types** - Checks each object part of "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`GqlResponse<User> & { payload: Input }`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n- 🎯 **Only your HyperFetch client** - "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`createClient`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " is checked when it comes from "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`@hyper-fetch/core`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": ", by name, alias\n  or namespace\n- 🔁 **Same rule names as ESLint** - "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`hyper-fetch/request-generic-types`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " and "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`hyper-fetch/client-generic-types`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n## 🚀 Quick Start\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```bash\nnpm install -D oxlint oxlint-plugin-hyper-fetch\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```json\n{\n  \"jsPlugins\": [\"oxlint-plugin-hyper-fetch\"],\n  \"rules\": {\n    \"hyper-fetch/client-generic-types\": \"error\",\n    \"hyper-fetch/request-generic-types\": \"error\"\n  }\n}\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n## 📚 Documentation\n\n- [Oxlint Plugin Docs](https://hyperfetch.bettertyped.com/docs/integrations/plugin-oxlint)\n- [Rules](https://hyperfetch.bettertyped.com/docs/integrations/plugin-oxlint/rules)\n- [Oxlint JS plugins](https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/linter/js-plugins)\n\n## 💡 Examples\n\n### Catches a misspelled generic\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```ts\n// ❌ hyper-fetch/request-generic-types: Unexpected generic type(s) found: rsponse\nconst getUser = client.createRequest<{ rsponse: User }>()({\n  endpoint: \"/users/:userId\",\n});\n\n// ✅\nconst getUser = client.createRequest<{ response: User }>()({\n  endpoint: \"/users/:userId\",\n});\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n### Checks composed generics part by part\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```ts\n// ❌ hyper-fetch/request-generic-types: Unexpected generic type(s) found: paylod\nconst updateUser = client.createRequest<GqlResponse<{ user: User }> & { paylod: UserInput }>()({\n  endpoint: updateUserMutation,\n});\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n## License\n\n[MIT](https://github.com/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch/blob/main/License.md)"
		}
	],
